==German==

===Etymology===
From northern {{inh|de|gmh|pissen}} and {{der|de|gml|pissen}}. Perhaps borrowed through {{der|de|dum|pissen}} from {{der|de|fro|pissier}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*pīssiō}}, probably of {{onomatopoeic|de|title=echoic}} origin, though the Germanic words are also sometimes considered independent {{onomatopoeic|de|title=onomatopoeias}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈpɪsən/|[ˈpɪsn̩]}}
* {{hyph|de|pis|sen}}
* {{audio|de|De-pissen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}} {{tlb|de|colloquial|slightly|vulgar}}

# to [[piss]] {{gloss|urinate}}
# to [[piss down]] {{gloss|rain heavily}}

